      "content": "That is a very strange way to characterize linguistic processes. Comparing grammatical suffixes to \"mischievous goblins\" or saying they \"play tricks\" is not standard academic terminology, and frankly, it's a bit unprofessional for a formal analysis.\n\nI am looking for a rigorous description of the phonological mechanisms, not a metaphorical narrative. Please set aside the goblin comparisons entirely and finish the analysis for \"lampi -> lammen.\" \n\nSpecifically, I need you to identify the actual consonant gradation occurring in the root \"lampi\" when the genitive suffix is applied, and explain the structural relationship between the stem and the suffix without using any whimsical language. Please be precise.",
